Notes are saved. The next question decides whether the induction-head idea has room to work: how open L15 H7's output gate already is at name positions. If it is already near 1 at the last name token, opening it further cannot add much stop signal. If it is mostly closed, as L19's heads were (about 0.2–0.4), there is room for a ×2–3 boost.

I'll compute L15 H7's gate values (mean sigmoid over its 256 gate rows) from the stored layer-15 inputs (`H2[:, 0]`, hidden index 15) and layers.15 q_proj / input_layernorm, at four kinds of positions:
- def positions;
- inner name positions;
- last name positions;
- ordinary positions.

I'll also print head 7's gate against the other heads of layer 15.

```python
# Hypothesis: L15H7 (induction head) has a mostly closed gate at name positions (room to amplify the '(' stop signal at the last name token).
Wq15 = load_original('model.language_model.layers.15.self_attn.q_proj.weight').numpy()
ln15 = load_original('model.language_model.layers.15.input_layernorm.weight').numpy()
def gate_at(hidx_arr, pl, W_, ln_):
    return np.stack([gates(hidx_arr[a_, b_].astype(np.float32), W_, ln_) for a_, b_ in pl])
h15 = H2[:, 0]
for lab, pl in [('def', def_pos[:200]), ('inner', inner_pos[:200]), ('last', list(last)[:200]), ('neg', list(neg[::200]))]:
    G15 = gate_at(h15, pl, Wq15, ln15)
    print('%-5s L15 gates per head: ' % lab + ' '.join('H%d %.2f' % (hh, G15[:, hh].mean()) for hh in range(8)))
```
